admin@dunbaroakshoa.com (use custom resource Lambda + SDK if required; include CloudFormation outputs for TXT values to add to DNS).\\\\n2. DynamoDB table DunbarOaksContactMessages (PK string, TS number) with PAY_PER_REQUEST billing, SSE enabled.\\\\n3. Final version of dhoa_contact.py Lambda (import from /lambda) that: • validates JSON input fields name, email, message • sends SES e-mail to admin@dunbaroakshoa.com • stores item in DynamoDB.\\\\n4. Grant minimal IAM permissions to the Lambda (ses:SendEmail, dynamodb:PutItem).\\\\n5. Outputs: ContactTableName, SesDomainIdentityArn.\\\\n\\\\nReturn REPORT sequence ID contact_resources_v1 containing overview, CDK file, Lambda code, and list of the DNS records administrators must publish.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 8,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"contact_resources_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_contact_v1###\\n\\n###order_security_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor – Produce security_stack.ts (CDK v2, TypeScript) that:\\\\n1. Enables GuardDuty detector in the current region.\\\\n2. Creates CloudTrail trail dhoa-org-trail with multi-region ON, delivering logs to dunbaroakshoa-logs bucket.\\\\n3. Enables AWS Config recorder with rules s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited and iam-user-no-policies.\\\\n4. Creates SNS topic SecurityAlerts and CloudWatch Metric/Alarm for GuardDuty ‘High’ findings >0 with e-mail subscription parameter.\\\\n5. Outputs: GuardDutyDetectorId, TrailArn, ConfigRecorderName, AlertsTopicArn.\\\\n\\\\nREPORT sequence ID security_stack_v1 with explanation and full file content.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 7,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"security_stack_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_security_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent A (11) is requesting approval for call ID cognito-001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need a specialized Attendant-rank agent to focus on implementing the Cognito CDK stack with all the specified requirements including User Pool, Identity Pool, IAM roles, and proper security configurations.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cognito CDK Implementation Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:33:22.508Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_cognito_v1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order cognito_stack_v1 from agent 11: **Cognito Authentication Stack Implementation Complete**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(a) **Brief Explanation:**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI have successfully created the CDK v2 TypeScript file `cognito_stack.ts` that implements a complete authentication and authorization infrastructure for the Dunbar Oaks HOA website. The implementation includes:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- A Cognito User Pool with email-based sign-up, optional MFA (TOTP + SMS), and strong password requirements\\\\\\\\n- Two user groups: 'residents' (default) and 'board_admins' with different privilege levels\\\\\\\\n- A Cognito Identity Pool federated with the User Pool for AWS service access\\\\\\\\n- Three IAM roles with least-privilege policies:\\\\\\\\n  - residents-role: Read-only access to private S3 documents\\\\\\\\n  - board-role: Full CRUD access to private S3 documents\\\\\\\\n  - unauth-role: No S3 access, only public API invocation\\\\\\\\n- All requested stack outputs for integration with other components\\\\\\\\n- Proper resource tagging for project organization\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe implementation uses group-based role mapping, ensuring board_admins automatically receive elevated permissions while maintaining security best practices.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(b) **Full File Content:**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```typescript\\\\\\\\nimport * as cdk from 'aws-cdk-lib';\\\\\\\\nimport { Stack, StackProps, CfnOutput, Tags } from 'aws-cdk-lib';\\\\\\\\nimport * as cognito from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-cognito';\\\\\\\\nimport * as iam from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-iam';\\\\\\\\nimport { Construct } from 'constructs';\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n/**\\\\\\\\n * CognitoStack provisions the authentication and authorization layer\\\\\\\\n * for the Dunbar Oaks HOA project, including:\\\\\\\\n *  - Cognito User Pool with best-practice configuration\\\\\\\\n *  - User groups (residents, board_admins)\\\\\\\\n *  - Cognito Identity Pool federated to the User Pool\\\\\\\\n *  - Least-privilege IAM roles for residents, board members & unauthenticated users\\\\\\\\n *  - Stack outputs for easy integration with other stacks / front-end\\\\\\\\n */\\\\\\\\nexport class CognitoStack extends Stack {\\\\\\\\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props?: StackProps) {\\\\\\\\n    super(scope, id, props);\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n     * 1. Cognito User Pool\\\\\\\\n     * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\\\\\\\n    const userPool = new cognito.UserPool(this, 'DunbarOaksResidentsPool', {\\\\\\\\n      userPoolName: 'DunbarOaksResidentsPool',\\\\\\\\n      // Email is the primary sign-in alias\\\\\\\\n      signInAliases: { email: true },\\\\\\\\n      selfSignUpEnabled: true,\\\\\\\\n      // Auto-verify emails so users must confirm ownership\\\\\\\\n      autoVerify: { email: true },\\\\\\\\n      // Strong password policy as requested\\\\\\\\n      passwordPolicy: {\\\\\\\\n        minLength: 8,\\\\\\\\n        requireLowercase: true,\\\\\\\\n        requireUppercase: true,\\\\\\\\n        requireDigits: true,\\\\\\\\n        requireSymbols: true,\\\\\\\\n      },\\\\\\\\n      // Optional MFA (both TOTP & SMS supported)\\\\\\\\n      mfa: cognito.Mfa.OPTIONAL,\\\\\\\\n      mfaSecondFactor: {\\\\\\\\n        otp: true,  // TOTP\\\\\\\\n        sms: true,  // SMS\\\\\\\\n      },\\\\\\\\n      // User accounts are retained by default; this can be adjusted if desired\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // App Client for Identity Pool federation & app authentication flows\\\\\\\\n    const userPoolClient = new cognito.UserPoolClient(this, 'UserPoolClient', {\\\\\\\\n      userPool,\\\\\\\\n      generateSecret: false, // Public client for web / mobile apps\\\\\\\\n      authFlows: {\\\\\\\\n        userPassword: true,\\\\\\\\n        userSrp: true,\\\\\\\\n      },\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n     * 2. User Groups\\\\\\\\n     * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\\\\\\\n    // Default residents group (all standard users)\\\\\\\\n    const residentsGroup = new cognito.CfnUserPoolGroup(this, 'ResidentsGroup', {\\\\\\\\n      groupName: 'residents',\\\\\\\\n      userPoolId: userPool.userPoolId,\\\\\\\\n      precedence: 10,\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // Elevated board_admins group\\\\\\\\n    const boardAdminsGroup = new cognito.CfnUserPoolGroup(this, 'BoardAdminsGroup', {\\\\\\\\n      groupName: 'board_admins',\\\\\\\\n      userPoolId: userPool.userPoolId,\\\\\\\\n      precedence: 0, // Higher priority (lower number) than residents\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n     * 3. Cognito Identity Pool\\\\\\\\n     * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\\\\\\\n    const identityPool = new cognito.CfnIdentityPool(this, 'DunbarOaksIdentityPool', {\\\\\\\\n      identityPoolName: 'DunbarOaksIdentityPool',\\\\\\\\n      allowUnauthenticatedIdentities: true,\\\\\\\\n      cognitoIdentityProviders: [\\\\\\\\n        {\\\\\\\\n          clientId: userPoolClient.userPoolClientId,\\\\\\\\n          providerName: userPool.userPoolProviderName,\\\\\\\\n          serverSideTokenCheck: true,\\\\\\\\n        },\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n     * 4. IAM Roles & Policies (Least Privilege)\\\\\\\\n     * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\\\\\\\n    const s3DocsPrefix = 'arn:aws:s3:::dunbaroakshoa-docs/private/*';\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // Common federated principal for Identity Pool roles\\\\\\\\n    const federatedPrincipal = (aud: string, amr: string) =>\\\\\\\\n      new iam.FederatedPrincipal(\\\\\\\\n        'cognito-identity.amazonaws.com',\\\\\\\\n        {\\\\\\\\n          'StringEquals': { 'cognito-identity.amazonaws.com:aud': aud },\\\\\\\\n          'ForAnyValue:StringLike': { 'cognito-identity.amazonaws.com:amr': amr },\\\\\\\\n        },\\\\\\\\n        'sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity',\\\\\\\\n      );\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // 4.a Residents (authenticated) – read-only S3 access\\\\\\\\n    const residentsRole = new iam.Role(this, 'ResidentsRole', {\\\\\\\\n      roleName: 'residents-role',\\\\\\\\n      assumedBy: federatedPrincipal(identityPool.ref, 'authenticated'),\\\\\\\\n      description: 'Read-only access for verified residents',\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n    residentsRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({\\\\\\\\n      actions: ['s3:GetObject'],\\\\\\\\n      resources: [s3DocsPrefix],\\\\\\\\n    }));\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // 4.b Board Admins – read/write/delete S3 access\\\\\\\\n    const boardRole = new iam.Role(this, 'BoardRole', {\\\\\\\\n      roleName: 'board-role',\\\\\\\\n      assumedBy: federatedPrincipal(identityPool.ref, 'authenticated'),\\\\\\\\n      description: 'Elevated S3 access for HOA board administrators',\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n    boardRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({\\\\\\\\n      actions: ['s3:GetObject', 's3:PutObject', 's3:DeleteObject'],\\\\\\\\n      resources: [s3DocsPrefix],\\\\\\\\n    }));\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    // 4.c Unauthenticated – no S3; public API invocation only (example permission)\\\\\\\\n    const unauthRole = new iam.Role(this, 'UnauthRole', {\\\\\\\\n      roleName: 'unauth-role',\\\\\\\\n      assumedBy: federatedPrincipal(identityPool.ref, 'unauthenticated'),\\\\\\\\n      description: 'Unauthenticated role with minimal permissions',\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\n    unauthRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({\\\\\\\\n      actions: ['execute-api:Invoke'],\\\\\\\\n      resources: ['arn:aws:execute-api:*:*:*'],\\\\\\\\n    }));\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n     * 5. Attach Roles to Identity Pool with Group-based Mapping\\\\\\\\n     * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\\\\\\\n    new cognito.CfnIdentityPoolRoleAttachment(this, 'IdentityPoolRoleAttachment', {\\\\\\\\n      identityPoolId: identityPool.ref,\\\\\\\\n      roles: {\\\\\\\\n        authenticated: residentsRole.roleArn,    // default for auth users\\\\\\\\n        unauthenticated: unauthRole.roleArn,     // unauth users\\\\\\\\n      },\\\\\\\\n      roleMappings: {\\\\\\\\n        BoardAdminsMapping: {\\\\\\\\n          type: 'Token',\\\\\\\\n          ambiguousRoleResolution: 'AuthenticatedRole', // fall back to residents-role\\\\\\\\n          identityProvider: `${userPool.userPoolProviderName}:${userPoolClient.userPoolClientId}`,\\\\\\\\n          rulesConfiguration: {\\\\\\\\n            rules: [\\\\\\\\n              {\\\\\\\\n                claim: 'cognito:groups',\\\\\\\\n                matchType: 'Contains',\\\\\\\\n                value: 'board_admins',\\\\\\\\n                roleArn: boardRole.roleArn,\\\\\\\\n              },\\\\\\\\n            ],\\\\\\\\n