onfiguration '{\\\\\\\"Rules\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"ApplyServerSideEncryptionByDefault\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"SSEAlgorithm\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AES256\\\\\\\"}}]}'\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket \\\\\\\"$DOCS_BUCKET\\\\\\\" --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-logging --bucket \\\\\\\"$DOCS_BUCKET\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --bucket-logging-status '{\\\\\\\"LoggingEnabled\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"TargetBucket\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"$LOGS_BUCKET\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TargetPrefix\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"docs/\\\\\\\"}}'\\\\naws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket \\\\\\\"$DOCS_BUCKET\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --public-access-block-configuration 'BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true'\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStep 3 – Deploy Cognito Stack via CloudFormation\\\\nCloudFormation template `cognito.yaml` (created by S-1) outputs \\\\nUserPoolId, IdentityPoolId, ResidentsRoleArn, BoardRoleArn.\\\\n```\\\\naws cloudformation deploy --stack-name cognito-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --template-file cognito.yaml --capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM\\\\nexport USER_POOL_ID=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name cognito-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query \\\\\\\"Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='UserPoolId'].OutputValue\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\nexport IDENTITY_POOL_ID=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name cognito-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query \\\\\\\"Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='IdentityPoolId'].OutputValue\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\nexport RESIDENTS_ROLE_ARN=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name cognito-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query \\\\\\\"Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='ResidentsRoleArn'].OutputValue\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\nexport BOARD_ROLE_ARN=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name cognito-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query \\\\\\\"Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='BoardRoleArn'].OutputValue\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStep 4 – Attach Docs-Bucket Policy referencing Cognito Roles (generated JSON)\\\\n```\\\\ncat > docsBucketPolicy.json <<EOF\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"AWS\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"$RESIDENTS_ROLE_ARN\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$BOARD_ROLE_ARN\\\\\\\"]},\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"s3:GetObject\\\\\\\"],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::$DOCS_BUCKET/private/*\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"AWS\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"$BOARD_ROLE_ARN\\\\\\\"},\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"s3:PutObject\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"s3:DeleteObject\\\\\\\"],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::$DOCS_BUCKET/private/*\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\nEOF\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-policy --bucket \\\\\\\"$DOCS_BUCKET\\\\\\\" --policy file://docsBucketPolicy.json\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStep 5 – Create DynamoDB Table (DunbarOaksContactMessages)\\\\n```\\\\naws dynamodb create-table \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --table-name DunbarOaksContactMessages \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --attribute-definitions AttributeName=PK,AttributeType=S AttributeName=TS,AttributeType=N \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --key-schema AttributeName=PK,KeyType=HASH AttributeName=TS,KeyType=RANGE \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStep 6 – Deploy API / Lambda Stack\\\\n(S-3 produces `api.yaml`; stack outputs RestApiId, ApiEndpoint)\\\\n```\\\\naws cloudformation deploy --stack-name api-stack --template-file api.yaml --capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM\\\\nexport API_ENDPOINT=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name api-stack \\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query \\\\\\\"Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='ApiEndpoint'].OutputValue\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nStep 7 – Verify SES Identities\\\\n```\\\\naws ses verify-domain-identity --domain \\\\\\\"$DOMAIN\\\\\\\"\\\\naws ses verify-email-identity --email-address \\\\\\\"$SES_EMAIL\\\\\\\"\\\\n```\\\\n*DNS TXT records returned from the first command must be added to Route 53 or external DNS; once in place, verification is automatic.*\\\\n\\\\nStep 8 – Deploy CI/CD Pipeline Stack (CICD)\\\\n```\\\\naws cloudformation deploy --stack-name cicd-stack --template-file cicd.yaml --capabilities CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM\\\\n```\\\\nPipeline then owns all future updates.\\\\n\\\\nStep 9 – Enable Security Services\\\\n```\\\\naws guardduty create-detector --enable\\\\naws cloudtrail create-trail --name dhoa-org-trail --s3-bucket-name \\\\\\\"$LOGS_BUCKET\\\\\\\" --is-multi-region-trail\\\\naws cloudtrail start-logging --name dhoa-org-trail\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nCompletion Criteria: no CLI errors, SES shows VERIFIED, API endpoint reachable, Cognito sign-up works.\\\\n\\\\n4. Clarifications Incorporated – none outstanding.\\\\n\\\\nEnd of updated plan.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_finalize_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###report_backend_finalize_v1###\\n\\n###recruit_s1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need a dedicated expert to translate Cognito/IAM portion of the architecture into CDK constructs and CloudFormation, ensuring least-privilege and alignment with Docs bucket policy.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CognitoIAMSupervisor\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit_s1###\\n\\n###order_s1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor – Create one file cognito_stack.ts (CDK v2, TypeScript) that synthesizes a CloudFormation template provisioning: (1) Cognito User Pool 'DunbarOaksResidentsPool' with email sign-up, optional MFA, resident and board_admin groups; (2) Cognito Identity Pool trusting that User Pool; (3) IAM Roles for residents, board_admins, and unauth; (4) Stack outputs for UserPoolId, IdentityPoolId, ResidentsRoleArn, BoardRoleArn.  Follow security best practices & tagging.  Once written, REPORT with sequence ID cognito_stack_v1 including a bri