ncurrent versions to Glacier after 30 days • block all public access.\\\\n3. Accept as props the ResidentsRoleArn and BoardRoleArn (CloudFormation parameters) and create a bucket policy granting the roles permissions identical to the design.\\\\n4. Outputs: DocsBucketName, LogsBucketName.\\\\n\\\\nReturn REPORT sequence ID s3_storage_v1 with explanation and file content.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 10,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"s3_storage_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_s3_v1###\\n\\n###order_api_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor – Deliver:\\\\n• api_stack.ts (CDK v2, TypeScript) defining REST API (regional) ‘DunbarOaksApi’ with resources /news [GET, NONE authorizer], /documents [GET, Cognito authorizer], /documents/{key} [GET, Cognito authorizer], /contact [POST, NONE].  Throttling: 100 r/s burst 200.  CORS for all origins allowed but headers restricted to Content-Type, Authorization.\\\\n• Four Lambda handler stubs in /lambda   dhoa_get_news.py, dhoa_list_docs.py, dhoa_presign.py, dhoa_contact.py – just placeholder logic returning 200 OK JSON.\\\\n• Integrations: Lambda proxy; Cognito authorizer wired to Identity Pool.\\\\n• IAM: grant lambdas minimum S3 & DynamoDB access via policies.\\\\n• Outputs: ApiEndpoint, RestApiId.\\\\n\\\\nREPORT with sequence ID api_stack_v1 including a summary and full code snippets for the TS stack file and the four handler stubs.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 9,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"api_stack_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_api_v1###\\n\\n###order_contact_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor – Provide contact_resources.ts (CDK v2, TypeScript) that accomplishes:\\\\n1. SES domain identity verification for dunbaroakshoa.com and e-mail identity admin@dunbaroakshoa.com (use custom resource Lambda + SDK if required; include CloudFormation outputs for TXT values to add to DNS).\\\\n2. DynamoDB table DunbarOaksContactMessages (PK string, TS